// THE DURABLE HALF OF THE APPROVAL LOOP: WHERE A REQUEST WAITS, WHERE A DECISION LANDS, AND THE
// KEY THAT MAKES A TAPPED LINK MEAN SOMETHING. gunbc.auth.approval_broker owns the lifecycle and
// gunbc.auth.approval_capability owns the signed link; neither can answer "what did the operator
// decide about escalation E" after the process that asked has exited, and the roadmap server's
// POST /approve/{capability} answered 501 for exactly that reason -- "the keyring, the decision
// store and the notification publisher are not deployed". This module is the keyring and the
// store. The publisher is gunbc.auth.approval_notification over the deployed ntfy server.
//
// THE LINK CARRIES A REFERENCE, NOT THE CLAIMS. The path segment is
// `<escalation_id>.<approve|deny>.<tag_hex>`: the server loads the claims it stored when the request
// was filed, re-derives approval_capability_signing_input over THOSE bytes, and verifies the tag
// against them. The tag still authenticates the whole claim set -- issuer, audience, authority,
// revision, decision, attempt, issued/expires, key id -- because it was computed over it; a forged
// id or a flipped decision fails the MAC. What this buys is that no URL-safe claims encoding is
// needed and the store is the one authority for what was asked, which the broker's one-commit law
// (approval_and_obligation_commit_together_note) already wants. verify_capability's join is
// unchanged: VerifiedMessage.message must equal the server's own signing input, byte for byte.
//
// WHAT THE STORE HOLDS PER ESCALATION IS ONE CAS SLOT, TWO GENERATIONS. Generation 1 is the filed
// request (the claims-grade facts and who asked); generation 2 is the decision WITH its execution
// obligation, in one commit. Approve and deny race for generation 2 and the CAS lets exactly one
// win; a second tap of either link finds generation 2 present and reports what was decided
// rather than deciding again. The subject and the scopes are NOT stored: they live with the
// workflow's own AuthorizationRequest<Subject> row in source, and the grant is derived by JOINING
// the stored decision to that row on escalation id and revision (the intent hash's wire form), so
// a decision can never be presented as consent for a different intent.

// ── the keyring ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// THE MAC KEY IS A SECRET MANAGER SECRET, MINTED 2026-09-16 UNDER OPERATOR AUTHORIZATION
// ("yes you can mint it"): 32 random bytes rendered as 64 lowercase hex, version 1 ENABLED, with
// roles/secretmanager.secretAccessor granted to fleet-cloud-convergence@gunbai-secrets only. The
// value never touched this repository or a session transcript; its sha256 prefix 113a3274bd95 is
// how a materialized copy is checked without printing it. Version is PINNED because a keyring that
// followed `latest` would let a rotation invalidate every link in flight (approval_capability:
// "key_id -- which key to check, so rotation does not invalidate what is in flight").
data approval_mac_key_secret_ref: SecretRef = secret_ref_pin_version(
  ref: fleet_secret_ref(secret_id: "approval-capability-mac-key"),
  version: "1",
)

data approval_mac_key_id: MacKeyId = "approval-capability-mac-key/1" as MacKeyId

data approval_mac_key_suite: MacSuite = HmacSha256

// WHERE THE KEY LIVES ON THE HOST THAT SERVES /approve: a file under the roadmap server's config
// directory, the same shape as /etc/gunbc-ntfy/publisher-token, written by fleet converge from the
// SecretRef above and readable by the unit's user only. The server reads the PATH from this row and
// the material into a Secret; nothing renders it. The converge step that writes the file is the
// declared frontier at the bottom of this module.
data approval_mac_key_path: NonEmptyStr = "/etc/gunbc-roadmap/approval-mac-key"

// ABSENT AND UNREADABLE ARE TWO REFUSALS WITH TWO REMEDIES (review 66990;
// extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io filesystem_absence_establishment_adoption_standing): an absent
// key means the materialization frontier has not run; an unreadable one means it ran and the unit
// cannot read what it wrote -- a permission on the file, not a missing step. Reading `content`
// alone and calling "" absent would report the second as the first, which fails toward good news.
// THE FAILURES ARE THEIR OWN COPRODUCT so a refusal downstream can carry exactly a failure and
// never the loaded key (review 67005: a refusal arm that could hold the success state validates
// instead of constructing).
type ApprovalKeyringRefusal
  = ApprovalKeyFileAbsent { path: NonEmptyStr }
  | ApprovalKeyFileUnreadable { path: NonEmptyStr, error: String }
  | ApprovalKeyMalformed { path: NonEmptyStr, length: Int }

type ApprovalKeyringRead
  = ApprovalKeyLoaded { key: MacKey }
  | ApprovalKeyringRefused { cause: ApprovalKeyringRefusal }

// Code points: '0'..'9' are 48..57, 'a'..'f' are 97..102.
fn is_lower_hex_code_point(cp: Int) -> Bool {
  (cp >= 48 && cp <= 57) || (cp >= 97 && cp <= 102)
}

fn is_lower_hex(s: String) -> Bool {
  all(s.chars(), cp => is_lower_hex_code_point(cp: cp))
}

// THE MATERIAL IS 64 LOWERCASE HEX DIGITS AND NOTHING ELSE; a trailing newline from an editor is
// refused rather than trimmed, because a key that verifies with one reader and not another is
// worse than one that refuses everywhere. An empty file is malformed, not absent: absence is the
// filesystem's answer, established by the exact read below, never inferred from empty content.
fn approval_keyring_from_content(content: String) -> ApprovalKeyringRead {
  if content.length() != 64 || !is_lower_hex(s: content) {
    ApprovalKeyringRefused { cause: ApprovalKeyMalformed { path: approval_mac_key_path, length: content.length() } }
  } else {
    ApprovalKeyLoaded { key: MacKey { id: approval_mac_key_id, suite: approval_mac_key_suite, material: content as Secret } }
  }
}

fn approval_keyring_from_exact_read(exact: FilesystemExactRead) -> ApprovalKeyringRead {
  match exact {
    FilesystemExactPathRead { path: _, content: c } => approval_keyring_from_content(content: c)
    FilesystemExactPathAbsent { path: _ } => ApprovalKeyringRefused { cause: ApprovalKeyFileAbsent { path: approval_mac_key_path } }
    FilesystemExactPathUnreadable { path: _, kind: _, error: e } => ApprovalKeyringRefused { cause: ApprovalKeyFileUnreadable { path: approval_mac_key_path, error: e } }
    FilesystemExactPathKindUnrecognized { path: _, observed: o, error: e } => ApprovalKeyringRefused { cause: ApprovalKeyFileUnreadable { path: approval_mac_key_path, error: concat(o, concat(": ", e)) } }
  }
}

fn read_approval_keyring() -> ApprovalKeyringRead {
  let read = Filesystem.Read(path: approval_mac_key_path as String)
  approval_keyring_from_exact_read(exact: filesystem_exact_read(path: approval_mac_key_path as String, content: read.content, success: read.success, error: read.error, error_kind: read.error_kind))
}

// ── what the verifier accepts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// THE EXPECTATION IS CONFIGURATION, NEVER READ FROM THE LINK (approval_capability
// CapabilityExpectation). Issuer is the process that mints links, audience is the broker that
// redeems them, authority is the one this store brokers for: operator consent to a fleet
// convergence step. A capability minted for another authority fails here on audience or
// authority before any decision is read.
data approval_capability_issuer: NonEmptyStr = "gunbc.roadmap_serve"
data approval_capability_audience: NonEmptyStr = "gunbc.auth.approval_broker"
data approval_capability_authority: NonEmptyStr = "gunbc.auth.scoped_authorization"

data approval_capability_expectation: CapabilityExpectation = CapabilityExpectation {
  issuer: approval_capability_issuer,
  audience: approval_capability_audience,
  authority: approval_capability_authority,
  suite: HmacSha256,
}

// THE OPERATOR IS ONE TAILNET LOGIN, and it is the row the fleet already owns:
// gunbc.fleet_posix_accounts fleet_operator_email, which the tailscale ACL consumes too. The
// live tailnet (`tailscale status` on srv1, 2026-09-16) reports the same login. A second literal
// here would be a second authority on who a tap may be (review 66990).
data approval_operator_login: NonEmptyStr = fleet_operator_email

// AND THE IDENTITY HEADER IS ONLY EVIDENCE WHEN THE BACKEND IS REACHABLE THROUGH TAILSCALE SERVE
// ALONE (extdeps.tailscale.identity identity_header_trust_is_a_deployment_property_note). The
// roadmap unit binds 0.0.0.0:8080 today. Until the deployment is loopback-only behind
// `tailscale serve`, a request that reaches the socket directly can present any login, and a
// redemption that trusted it would report the operator's consent for something they never saw.
// So the store refuses to redeem unless the deployment property is DECLARED established, and the
// declaration is a row a deploy change flips with its evidence -- not a flag a handler defaults.
type IdentityTrustStanding
  = IdentityHeaderTrustEstablished { evidence: NonEmptyStr }
  | IdentityHeaderTrustNotEstablished { blocker: NonEmptyStr }

data approval_identity_trust: IdentityTrustStanding = IdentityHeaderTrustNotEstablished {
  blocker: "gunbc-roadmap.service binds 0.0.0.0:8080 (systemctl cat, srv1, 2026-09-16); the Tailscale-User-Login header is self-asserted by anything that reaches that socket. Established when the unit binds 127.0.0.1 and tailscale serve is the only path in, recorded here with the unit file digest and the serve config as evidence.",
}

// ── the store ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// CONSENT RECORDS ARE AUTHORIZATION STATE, so every generation is published OWNER-ONLY
// (OwnerOnlyCreateOnly -> Filesystem.WriteOwnerOnly, 0600): the rule gunbc.durable_cas_file_store
// states for a bare path with no directory-mode authority (review 66990). A record names who asked,
// for what, whether it is destructive and who decided; none of that is for other users of the host.
data approval_decision_store_root: NonEmptyStr = "/var/lib/gunbc/approvals"

// THE CLAIMS-GRADE FACTS OF A FILED REQUEST. Everything approval_capability_signing_input reads is
// here except the decision, which is what the two links differ in; requester, purpose and
// destructive are what the operator READS on the confirmation page and what admission checked
// before the notification went out.
type StoredApprovalRequest {
  escalation_id: NonEmptyStr
  request_revision: NonEmptyStr
  attempt: AttemptIdentity
  requester: NonEmptyStr
  purpose: NonEmptyStr
  destructive: Bool
  issued_at: Timestamp
  expires_at: Timestamp
  key_id: MacKeyId
}

fn stored_request_json(r: StoredApprovalRequest) -> String {
  serialize_json(v: json_object(members: [
    json_kv(key: "kind", value: json_string(s: "request")),
    json_kv(key: "escalation_id", value: json_string(s: r.escalation_id as String)),
    json_kv(key: "request_revision", value: json_string(s: r.request_revision as String)),
    json_kv(key: "attempt", value: json_string(s: r.attempt as String)),
    json_kv(key: "requester", value: json_string(s: r.requester as String)),
    json_kv(key: "purpose", value: json_string(s: r.purpose as String)),
    json_kv(key: "destructive", value: json_bool(b: r.destructive)),
    json_kv(key: "issued_at", value: json_string(s: r.issued_at)),
    json_kv(key: "expires_at", value: json_string(s: r.expires_at)),
    json_kv(key: "key_id", value: json_string(s: r.key_id as String)),
  ]))
}

fn stored_decision_json(d: BrokerDecision) -> String {
  match d {
    BrokerApproved { escalation_id: e, revision: r, decided_by: by, decided_at: at, obligation: o } =>
      serialize_json(v: json_object(members: [
        json_kv(key: "kind", value: json_string(s: "approved")),
        json_kv(key: "escalation_id", value: json_string(s: e as String)),
        json_kv(key: "revision", value: json_string(s: r as String)),
        json_kv(key: "decided_by", value: json_string(s: by as String)),
        json_kv(key: "decided_at", value: json_string(s: at)),
        json_kv(key: "obligation_authority", value: json_string(s: o.authority as String)),
        json_kv(key: "obligation_intent_revision", value: json_string(s: o.intent_revision as String)),
        json_kv(key: "obligation_execute_by", value: json_string(s: o.execute_by)),
      ]))
    BrokerDenied { escalation_id: e, revision: r, decided_by: by, decided_at: at, reason: why } =>
      serialize_json(v: json_object(members: [
        json_kv(key: "kind", value: json_string(s: "denied")),
        json_kv(key: "escalation_id", value: json_string(s: e as String)),
        json_kv(key: "revision", value: json_string(s: r as String)),
        json_kv(key: "decided_by", value: json_string(s: by as String)),
        json_kv(key: "decided_at", value: json_string(s: at)),
        json_kv(key: "reason", value: json_string(s: why as String)),
      ]))
  }
}

// ── reading a record back ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

type JsonFieldRead
  = FieldString { value: String }
  | FieldBool { value: Bool }
  | FieldMissing { key: String }

fn json_field(v: JsonValue, key: String) -> JsonFieldRead {
  match json_object_unique_member(v: v, key: key) {
    JsonMemberFound { value: JsonString { value: s } } => FieldString { value: s }
    JsonMemberFound { value: JsonBool { value: b } } => FieldBool { value: b }
    JsonMemberFound { value: _ } => FieldMissing { key: key }
    JsonMemberAbsent => FieldMissing { key: key }
    JsonMemberDuplicated { count: _ } => FieldMissing { key: key }
    JsonMemberNotAnObject => FieldMissing { key: key }
  }
}

fn json_field_string(v: JsonValue, key: String) -> String? {
  match json_field(v: v, key: key) {
    FieldString { value: s } => if s == "" { none } else { Present { value: s } }
    _ => none
  }
}

fn json_field_bool(v: JsonValue, key: String) -> Bool? {
  match json_field(v: v, key: key) {
    FieldBool { value: b } => Present { value: b }
    _ => none
  }
}

type StoredRecordParse
  = StoredRequestParsed { request: StoredApprovalRequest }
  | StoredDecisionParsed { decision: BrokerDecision }
  | StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: NonEmptyStr }

fn parse_stored_request(v: JsonValue) -> StoredRecordParse {
  match json_field_string(v: v, key: "escalation_id") {
    Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored request lacks escalation_id" }
    Present { value: e } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "request_revision") {
      Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored request lacks request_revision" }
      Present { value: rev } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "attempt") {
        Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored request lacks attempt" }
        Present { value: att } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "requester") {
          Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored request lacks requester" }
          Present { value: req } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "purpose") {
            Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored request lacks purpose" }
            Present { value: purpose } => match json_field_bool(v: v, key: "destructive") {
              Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored request lacks destructive" }
              Present { value: destructive } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "issued_at") {
                Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored request lacks issued_at" }
                Present { value: issued } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "expires_at") {
                  Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored request lacks expires_at" }
                  Present { value: expires } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "key_id") {
                    Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored request lacks key_id" }
                    Present { value: kid } => StoredRequestParsed { request: StoredApprovalRequest {
                      escalation_id: e as NonEmptyStr,
                      request_revision: rev as NonEmptyStr,
                      attempt: att as AttemptIdentity,
                      requester: req as NonEmptyStr,
                      purpose: purpose as NonEmptyStr,
                      destructive: destructive,
                      issued_at: issued,
                      expires_at: expires,
                      key_id: kid as MacKeyId,
                    } }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

fn parse_stored_decision(v: JsonValue, kind: String) -> StoredRecordParse {
  match json_field_string(v: v, key: "escalation_id") {
    Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored decision lacks escalation_id" }
    Present { value: e } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "revision") {
      Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored decision lacks revision" }
      Present { value: rev } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "decided_by") {
        Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored decision lacks decided_by" }
        Present { value: by } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "decided_at") {
          Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored decision lacks decided_at" }
          Present { value: at } =>
            if kind == "approved" {
              match json_field_string(v: v, key: "obligation_authority") {
                Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored approval lacks obligation_authority" }
                Present { value: oa } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "obligation_intent_revision") {
                  Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored approval lacks obligation_intent_revision" }
                  Present { value: oi } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "obligation_execute_by") {
                    Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored approval lacks obligation_execute_by" }
                    Present { value: ob } => StoredDecisionParsed { decision: BrokerApproved {
                      escalation_id: e as NonEmptyStr, revision: rev as NonEmptyStr, decided_by: by as NonEmptyStr, decided_at: at,
                      obligation: ExecutionObligation { authority: oa as NonEmptyStr, intent_revision: oi as NonEmptyStr, execute_by: ob },
                    } }
                  }
                }
              }
            } else {
              match json_field_string(v: v, key: "reason") {
                Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored denial lacks reason" }
                Present { value: why } => StoredDecisionParsed { decision: BrokerDenied {
                  escalation_id: e as NonEmptyStr, revision: rev as NonEmptyStr, decided_by: by as NonEmptyStr, decided_at: at, reason: why as NonEmptyStr,
                } }
              }
            }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

fn parse_stored_record(text: String) -> StoredRecordParse {
  match parse_json_document(s: text) {
    JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap: _ } => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored record is not a JSON document" }
    JsonDocumentParsed { value: v } => match json_field_string(v: v, key: "kind") {
      Absent => StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: "stored record lacks kind" }
      Present { value: kind } =>
        if kind == "request" { parse_stored_request(v: v) }
        else if kind == "approved" || kind == "denied" { parse_stored_decision(v: v, kind: kind) }
        else { StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: concat("stored record kind is not request, approved or denied: ", kind) as NonEmptyStr } }
    }
  }
}

// THE SLOT AS THE BROKER SEES IT: nothing filed, a request waiting at generation 1, a decision at
// generation 2, or a store that could not be read -- four states, none collapsed into another.
type EscalationSlot
  = EscalationNotFiled
  | EscalationPending { request: StoredApprovalRequest }
  | EscalationDecided { decision: BrokerDecision }
  | EscalationUnreadable { detail: NonEmptyStr }

fn observe_escalation(root: NonEmptyStr, escalation_id: NonEmptyStr) -> EscalationSlot {
  match observe_cas_slot_state(root: root, key: escalation_id) {
    CasObservedUnreadable { cause: _ } => EscalationUnreadable { detail: "approval store slot unreadable" }
    CasObservedReadable { readable: r } => match r {
      CasReadableAbsent => EscalationNotFiled
      CasReadablePresent { version: v } => match parse_stored_record(text: v.value as String) {
        StoredRecordUnreadable { detail: d } => EscalationUnreadable { detail: d }
        StoredRequestParsed { request: req } =>
          if cas_generation_count(g: v.generation) == 1 { EscalationPending { request: req } }
          else { EscalationUnreadable { detail: "a request record sits above generation 1" } }
        StoredDecisionParsed { decision: d } =>
          if cas_generation_count(g: v.generation) == 2 { EscalationDecided { decision: d } }
          else { EscalationUnreadable { detail: "a decision record sits at a generation other than 2" } }
      }
    }
  }
}

// ── filing and deciding ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

type StoreWrite
  = StoreWritten
  | StoreSlotOccupied
  | StoreRefused { detail: NonEmptyStr }

fn store_write_from_cas(outcome: CasOutcome<NonEmptyStr>) -> StoreWrite {
  match outcome {
    CasCommitted { committed: _ } => StoreWritten
    CasPreconditionFailed { expected: _, observed: _ } => StoreSlotOccupied
    CasStoreRefused { cause: _ } => StoreRefused { detail: "approval store refused the publication" }
  }
}

// GENERATION 1: THE REQUEST. ExpectSlotAbsent, so a second filing under the same escalation id
// reports occupied rather than overwriting what the operator may already have been shown.
fn file_approval_request(root: NonEmptyStr, request: StoredApprovalRequest) -> StoreWrite {
  let payload = stored_request_json(r: request) as NonEmptyStr
  match admit_cas_attempt_for_derived_payload(key: request.escalation_id, expected: ExpectSlotAbsent, proposed: payload) {
    DerivedPayloadKeyNotSlotAddressable { key: _ } => StoreRefused { detail: "escalation id is not slot-addressable" }
    DerivedPayloadAdmitted { verified: v } =>
      store_write_from_cas(outcome: file_compare_and_set(root: root, publication: OwnerOnlyCreateOnly, verified: v))
  }
}

// GENERATION 2: THE DECISION AND ITS OBLIGATION, ONE COMMIT, expecting generation 1 -- so approve
// and deny cannot both win, and a decision cannot land on an escalation nobody filed.
fn commit_broker_decision(root: NonEmptyStr, decision: BrokerDecision) -> StoreWrite {
  let escalation_id = match decision {
    BrokerApproved { escalation_id: e, revision: _, decided_by: _, decided_at: _, obligation: _ } => e
    BrokerDenied { escalation_id: e, revision: _, decided_by: _, decided_at: _, reason: _ } => e
  }
  let payload = stored_decision_json(d: decision) as NonEmptyStr
  match admit_cas_attempt_for_derived_payload(key: escalation_id, expected: ExpectSlotGeneration { generation: cas_generation_first() }, proposed: payload) {
    DerivedPayloadKeyNotSlotAddressable { key: _ } => StoreRefused { detail: "escalation id is not slot-addressable" }
    DerivedPayloadAdmitted { verified: v } =>
      store_write_from_cas(outcome: file_compare_and_set(root: root, publication: OwnerOnlyCreateOnly, verified: v))
  }
}

// ── the link ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// THE CLAIMS A STORED REQUEST STANDS FOR, under one proposed decision. The two links a request
// gets differ only in this field, so they carry different tags.
fn claims_for(request: StoredApprovalRequest, decision: ProposedDecision) -> ApprovalCapabilityClaims {
  ApprovalCapabilityClaims {
    protocol: "gunbc.approval-capability.v1",
    issuer: approval_capability_issuer,
    audience: approval_capability_audience,
    authority: approval_capability_authority,
    escalation_id: request.escalation_id,
    request_revision: request.request_revision,
    decision: decision,
    attempt: request.attempt,
    issued_at: request.issued_at,
    expires_at: request.expires_at,
    key_id: request.key_id,
  }
}

data capability_segment_separator: String = "."

fn capability_path_segment(escalation_id: NonEmptyStr, decision: ProposedDecision, tag_hex: NonEmptyStr) -> NonEmptyStr {
  join([escalation_id as String, proposed_decision_name(d: decision) as String, tag_hex as String], capability_segment_separator) as NonEmptyStr
}

type CapabilitySegmentParse
  = CapabilitySegmentParsed { escalation_id: NonEmptyStr, decision: ProposedDecision, tag_hex: NonEmptyStr }
  | CapabilitySegmentMalformed { detail: NonEmptyStr }

// THE ESCALATION ID MAY NOT CONTAIN THE SEPARATOR; that is the price of a three-part segment and
// it is checked at filing time by cas_key_is_slot_addressable's caller, and again here on the way
// in so a crafted id cannot shift the decision word.
fn parse_capability_segment(segment: String) -> CapabilitySegmentParse {
  let parts = segment.split(sep: capability_segment_separator)
  if count(parts) != 3 {
    CapabilitySegmentMalformed { detail: "capability segment is not <escalation_id>.<decision>.<tag_hex>" }
  } else {
    let e = match parts.first() { Present { value: v } => v Absent => "" }
    let d = match parts.skip(n: 1).first() { Present { value: v } => v Absent => "" }
    let t = match parts.skip(n: 2).first() { Present { value: v } => v Absent => "" }
    if e == "" || t == "" {
      CapabilitySegmentMalformed { detail: "capability segment has an empty escalation id or tag" }
    } else if d == (proposed_decision_name(d: ProposeApprove) as String) {
      CapabilitySegmentParsed { escalation_id: e as NonEmptyStr, decision: ProposeApprove, tag_hex: t as NonEmptyStr }
    } else if d == (proposed_decision_name(d: ProposeDeny) as String) {
      CapabilitySegmentParsed { escalation_id: e as NonEmptyStr, decision: ProposeDeny, tag_hex: t as NonEmptyStr }
    } else {
      CapabilitySegmentMalformed { detail: concat("capability segment decision word is not approve or deny: ", d) as NonEmptyStr }
    }
  }
}

// ── redemption over the store ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// EVERY WAY A TAP CAN END, each located. RedeemedApproved and RedeemedDenied are the two facts a
// tap can establish; AlreadyDecided is what a second tap sees; everything else is a refusal with
// the layer that refused named in the arm.
type StoreRedemption
  = RedeemedApproved { decision: BrokerDecision }
  | RedeemedDenied { decision: BrokerDecision }
  | AlreadyDecided { decision: BrokerDecision }
  | RedemptionSegmentMalformed { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | RedemptionEscalationNotFiled { escalation_id: NonEmptyStr }
  | RedemptionStoreUnreadable { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | RedemptionKeyringUnavailable { cause: ApprovalKeyringRefusal }
  | RedemptionIdentityUntrusted { blocker: NonEmptyStr }
  | RedemptionBrokerRefused { cause: RedemptionRefusal }
  | RedemptionLostTheRace
  | RedemptionCommitRefused { detail: NonEmptyStr }

fn store_redemption_reason(r: StoreRedemption) -> String {
  match r {
    RedeemedApproved { decision: _ } => "approved and recorded"
    RedeemedDenied { decision: _ } => "denied and recorded"
    AlreadyDecided { decision: _ } => "this escalation was already decided; nothing changed"
    RedemptionSegmentMalformed { detail: d } => d as String
    RedemptionEscalationNotFiled { escalation_id: e } => concat("no request is filed under escalation ", e as String)
    RedemptionStoreUnreadable { detail: d } => concat("approval store unreadable: ", d as String)
    RedemptionKeyringUnavailable { cause: k } => match k {
      ApprovalKeyFileAbsent { path: p } => concat("approval MAC key file is absent: ", p as String)
      ApprovalKeyFileUnreadable { path: p, error: e } => concat("approval MAC key file is unreadable: ", concat(p as String, concat(" -- ", e)))
      ApprovalKeyMalformed { path: p, length: n } => concat("approval MAC key file is malformed (", concat(to_string(n), concat(" chars): ", p as String)))
    }
    RedemptionIdentityUntrusted { blocker: b } => concat("the identity header cannot be trusted on this deployment: ", b as String)
    RedemptionBrokerRefused { cause: c } => redemption_refusal_reason(r: c)
    RedemptionLostTheRace => "another decision landed first; this tap changed nothing"
    RedemptionCommitRefused { detail: d } => concat("decision could not be committed: ", d as String)
  }
}

// THE ONE FOLD BEHIND POST /approve/{capability}. Order: the deployment must vouch for the
// identity header at all; the segment must parse; the escalation must be filed and pending; the
// keyring must load; then the broker decides (MAC over the STORED claims first, then policy, then
// identity); and only an admitted redemption is committed, with the obligation, at generation 2.
// A second tap lands on AlreadyDecided before the MAC is even checked -- there is nothing left to
// decide and no oracle in saying so, since the store's own state is not a secret. The obligation's
// execute_by is the filed request's own lifetime: the operator approved THAT window, and a
// separate deadline supplied at tap time would be a second authority on how long consent lasts.
fn redeem_over_store(
  root: NonEmptyStr,
  trust: IdentityTrustStanding,
  keyring: ApprovalKeyringRead,
  method: HttpMethod,
  segment: String,
  presented_identity: TailnetIdentity,
  observed_at: Timestamp,
) -> StoreRedemption {
  match trust {
    IdentityHeaderTrustNotEstablished { blocker: b } => RedemptionIdentityUntrusted { blocker: b }
    IdentityHeaderTrustEstablished { evidence: _ } =>
      match parse_capability_segment(segment: segment) {
        CapabilitySegmentMalformed { detail: d } => RedemptionSegmentMalformed { detail: d }
        CapabilitySegmentParsed { escalation_id: e, decision: proposed, tag_hex: tag } =>
          match observe_escalation(root: root, escalation_id: e) {
            EscalationNotFiled => RedemptionEscalationNotFiled { escalation_id: e }
            EscalationUnreadable { detail: d } => RedemptionStoreUnreadable { detail: d }
            EscalationDecided { decision: d } => AlreadyDecided { decision: d }
            EscalationPending { request: req } =>
              match keyring {
                ApprovalKeyLoaded { key: key } => {
                  let claims = claims_for(request: req, decision: proposed)
                  let mac_result: MacVerification = mac_verify(key: key, message: approval_capability_signing_input(c: claims), tag_hex: tag)
                  match redeem_capability(
                    method: method,
                    capability: ApprovalCapability { claims: claims, tag_b64url: tag },
                    expectation: approval_capability_expectation,
                    mac_result: mac_result,
                    presented_identity: presented_identity,
                    expected_operator: approval_operator_login,
                    observed_at: observed_at,
                  ) {
                    RedemptionRefused { cause: c } => RedemptionBrokerRefused { cause: c }
                    RedemptionAdmitted { claims: cl, decided_by: by } => {
                      let decision = match cl.decision {
                        ProposeApprove => BrokerApproved {
                          escalation_id: cl.escalation_id, revision: cl.request_revision, decided_by: by, decided_at: observed_at,
                          obligation: ExecutionObligation { authority: cl.authority, intent_revision: cl.request_revision, execute_by: req.expires_at },
                        }
                        ProposeDeny => BrokerDenied {
                          escalation_id: cl.escalation_id, revision: cl.request_revision, decided_by: by, decided_at: observed_at,
                          reason: "denied by the operator through the approval link",
                        }
                      }
                      match commit_broker_decision(root: root, decision: decision) {
                        StoreWritten => match decision {
                          BrokerApproved { escalation_id: _, revision: _, decided_by: _, decided_at: _, obligation: _ } => RedeemedApproved { decision: decision }
                          BrokerDenied { escalation_id: _, revision: _, decided_by: _, decided_at: _, reason: _ } => RedeemedDenied { decision: decision }
                        }
                        StoreSlotOccupied => RedemptionLostTheRace
                        StoreRefused { detail: d } => RedemptionCommitRefused { detail: d }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
                ApprovalKeyringRefused { cause: c } => RedemptionKeyringUnavailable { cause: c }
              }
          }
      }
  }
}

// ── the grant a workflow receives ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// THE JOIN THAT TURNS A STORED DECISION INTO CONSENT FOR ONE INTENT. The workflow supplies its
// own AuthorizationRequest<Subject> (subject, scopes, intent hash) from source; the store supplies
// the decision. They agree only when escalation id AND revision -- the intent hash's wire form --
// match; otherwise the decision is somebody else's and the grant is refused. A pending or absent
// slot yields the request's own AuthorizationPending, so a workflow polling the store sees the
// same value it would have declared by hand, and the srv3 source-declared grant
// (gunbc.srv3_os_install_actuate_workflow srv3_boot_once_cd_source_declared_grant_dissolve_on)
// dissolves into this fold.
type GrantDerivation<Subject>
  = GrantDerived { authorization: ScopedAuthorization<Subject> }
  | GrantStillPending { escalation_id: NonEmptyStr }
  | GrantEscalationNotFiled { escalation_id: NonEmptyStr }
  | GrantForAnotherIntent { requested_revision: NonEmptyStr, decided_revision: NonEmptyStr }
  | GrantStoreUnreadable { detail: NonEmptyStr }

fn request_revision_of<Subject>(request: AuthorizationRequest<Subject>) -> NonEmptyStr {
  serialize_content_hash(hash: request.intent_hash)
}

fn grant_from_store<Subject>(root: NonEmptyStr, request: AuthorizationRequest<Subject>) -> GrantDerivation<Subject> {
  let revision = request_revision_of(request: request)
  match observe_escalation(root: root, escalation_id: request.escalation_id) {
    EscalationNotFiled => GrantEscalationNotFiled { escalation_id: request.escalation_id }
    EscalationUnreadable { detail: d } => GrantStoreUnreadable { detail: d }
    EscalationPending { request: _ } => GrantStillPending { escalation_id: request.escalation_id }
    EscalationDecided { decision: d } => match d {
      BrokerApproved { escalation_id: e, revision: r, decided_by: by, decided_at: at, obligation: o } =>
        if e != request.escalation_id || r != revision {
          GrantForAnotherIntent { requested_revision: revision, decided_revision: r }
        } else {
          GrantDerived { authorization: AuthorizationGranted {
            grant: OperatorGrant {
              escalation_id: request.escalation_id,
              scopes: request.scopes,
              subject: request.subject,
              purpose: request.purpose,
              attempt: request.attempt,
              intent_hash: request.intent_hash,
              granted_by: by,
              granted_at: at,
              expires_at: o.execute_by,
            },
            claim: Unclaimed,
          } }
        }
      BrokerDenied { escalation_id: e, revision: r, decided_by: by, decided_at: at, reason: why } =>
        if e != request.escalation_id || r != revision {
          GrantForAnotherIntent { requested_revision: revision, decided_revision: r }
        } else {
          GrantDerived { authorization: AuthorizationDenied { escalation_id: e, denied_by: by, denied_at: at, reason: why } }
        }
    }
  }
}

// ── the frontiers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ISSUANCE: minting the two links for a filed request needs a MAC tag, and the substrate can only
// verify one today (extdeps.crypto.mac: hmac_sha256_verify_hex, no signing primitive). The
// consumer that files a request and publishes the notification with the signed URL is the next
// change, gated on that primitive.
data approval_issuance_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "a MAC issuance primitive (hmac_sha256_hex) and extdeps.crypto.mac mac_sign, so that gunbc.auth.approval_capability can mint an ApprovalCapability for claims_for(request, ProposeApprove) and claims_for(request, ProposeDeny) -- SUFFICIENT FOR filing a request into this store and publishing gunbc.auth.approval_notification with capability_path_segment links; in flight as the approval-loop part A lane (eager-owl-205, 2026-09-16). NOT satisfied by a hand-computed tag committed as a fixture, which is what the witness uses to exercise the verify side until then.",
)

// THE KEY ON THE HOST: fleet converge materializes approval_mac_key_secret_ref into
// approval_mac_key_path, 0640, owned by root and readable by the roadmap unit's user, the same
// shape as /etc/gunbc-ntfy/publisher-token. Until that step exists the keyring reads absent and
// every redemption refuses RedemptionKeyringUnavailable -- loud, never a fabricated key.
data approval_keyring_materialization_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "a fleet-converge step that reads approval_mac_key_secret_ref through the WIF-backed convergence account and writes approval_mac_key_path (0640 root:<roadmap unit user>) on the host that serves /approve, with the file's sha256 compared to the store's payload -- SUFFICIENT FOR read_approval_keyring to load the key on srv1; the same step is the model for GUNBC_HOST_RESET_BMC_CREDENTIAL_FILE materialization in gunbc.host.host_reset_return_run.",
)
